{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1377771-how-to-build-pc-level-npcs-correctly","id":1377771,"title":"How to build pc level Npcs correctly","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-01T11:53:44-07:00","id":1377771,"title":"How to build pc level Npcs correctly","content":"I'm working on a Supplement for Scion and am trying to figure how to build npc's. Does anyone have an idea of how much XP your supposed to have per dot of legend or a rough ballpark of how many extra dots to give a legend 2 or 3 scion. Any help would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25109-dreamer1331","name":"dreamer1331","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T12:01:17-07:00","id":1377774,"title":"","content":"I'd suggest reading the Antagonists chapter in Origin again. Build your NPCs with that framework. There is no need to fully stat out an NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T12:07:25-07:00","id":1377775,"title":"","content":"Yeah, echoing Florin. A decently built antagonist isn't really weaker than a PC, just a lot simpler","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T12:27:49-07:00","id":1377781,"title":"","content":"Ive read that chapter. The thing I'm trying to figure out is pc scale. Like how much xp does a legend 4 scion have to buy things like followers or relics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25109-dreamer1331","name":"dreamer1331","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T13:30:00-07:00","id":1377790,"title":"","content":"That's going to vary a lot from game to game. Honestly, I'd look more to things like actual Scale. A Legend 4 Scion can pull off Scale 3 actions. So, that's something the NPC should be able to handle. Followers and relics are probably going to pale to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8719,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","user":"Florin","date":". 04-01-2020, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T14:00:56-07:00","id":1377794,"title":"","content":"Like ideally you shouldn't be statting an NPC with a full PC writeup.<br /> <br /> &quot;How much Doodads should they have?&quot; - How many do they need? How many is too much that it becomes a pain.<br /> <br /> &quot;What should their Relics do?&quot; - What they need to. If a PC scavenges the Relic then maybe stat it up really quickly.<br /> <br /> &quot;What Boons should they have?&quot; - Which ones do you need them to know?<br /> <br /> Also things to ask yourself: Will this NPC even need stats? Like, if a Guide is being used, I generally don't stat them up. Because when will they need to roll dice? Almost never, that's when. They talk to the PC and give them advice.<br /> <br /> If it's an antagonist, just use the antagonist rules. Antagonists <i>don't need</i> as many notes about their stats as PCs do, because NPCs are usually created with a few uses in mind.<br /> <br /> Even antagonist Scions don't need full PC writeups. Like, if you need your PCs to run into a combat-focused Scion, pick the Rival or Nemesis Archetype, add the relevant Flairs or Qualities to represent their tricks, maybe give them a Relic that gives them access to a Purview or some Enhancement. Boom, done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 04-01-2020, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T10:25:41-07:00","id":1378302,"title":"","content":"ok let me rephrase the question. I need help building pre gen characters at above legend 1 and would like a rough idea for how much xp per legend","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25109-dreamer1331","name":"dreamer1331","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T10:39:12-07:00","id":1378306,"title":"","content":"What sounds like a reasonable number of sessions per band deed? Personally, I'd say 10-15, if I was using my Aeon game (which does not have anything like Legend in it) as a guide. (That seems to be about how long a single story/quest line has lasted.) The average is about 5 xp per game. So, I'd say about 50 xp per legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8719,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","user":"Florin","date":". 04-03-2020, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T11:34:09-07:00","id":1378310,"title":"","content":"Oooh, pregen characters. In my experience one can accumulate like 40-50 xp between each Legend Dot, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T11:52:32-07:00","id":1378313,"title":"","content":"ok 40-50 was close to my guys of about 35. thanks 